Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_WRITES=1: while a guard is up, a guest write to any page the caches track is copied first; off by default

T91 and T94, six door runs with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3 (three plain, two with 16-page granules,
one with 64): fade in order in 6 of 6, the cut to Link's house clean in 5 of 6, speed as the
control (17.1-18.1 fps against 17.4), but three single dark frames were left (50 ms, 70-109
cells each); the controls have two to four longer moments a run. Wider granules did not change
that.

The guard copies the pages it guessed. A clean page the guess missed is not copied, although its
write comes through HandleRasterizerWrite anyway (the caches trap the pages they hold clean).
With this switch such a write copies its page first too: the copy serves the GPU thread's
buffer reads, and with =3 the write then reaches the caches (buffer mark, inline upload, texture
re-upload) only after the frame's fence. No extra trap; a page of this kind takes no room once
the pool is full.

---
