+/// EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_WRITES=1 (with =2 or =3): while a guard is up, a guest write to ANY
+/// page the caches track is copied first, not only to the pages the guard guessed. Such a write
+/// comes through HandleRasterizerWrite anyway (the buffer, texture and shader caches trap the
+/// pages they hold clean), so this costs the 4 KiB copy and no trap. It covers a clean page the
+/// guess missed: its copy serves the GPU thread's reads, and with =3 the write reaches the caches
+/// (buffer mark, inline upload, texture re-upload) only after the fence. T91/T94, six door runs
+/// with =3: three single dark frames were left (the control has two to four longer moments a
+/// run). A page of this kind takes no room once the pool is full: it is left as before.
+inline bool AllWrites() {
+    static const bool on = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_WRITES");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1' && value[1] == '\0';
+    }();
+    return on;
+}
